Well, my second MR-less, wishless attempt nearly got stuck between 
Medusa's and the Caslte.

Another Valkyrie, this time human lawful (lst one was dwarvish), so in a 
pinch, the MMF's might all just silently vanish and disapear... XL 13 
(going 14, #twoweaponing the blessed rustproof +1 Excalibur and a silver 
saber (to get the neccessary skills up for Gehennom)).

Here's the tale of stupidity and luck at the Castle. Yesterday, I 
decided to see how deep I can go before doing the Quest (I had planned 
on reaching Medusa, then back up, do some more monster slaying for XP to 
reach XL 14 and then go have a violent argument with Lord Sutur about a 
certain orb).

Well, not much interesting happened, until I stepped three steps away 
from the stairs on Medusa's level (the non-Titan variant) and promptly 
fell down a trap door, which dropped me right in front of the castle.

Not too bad, the L's didn't bother me much (only simple ones in the 
castle, don't know if there was an arch-lich, but I rather doubt it) and 
they didn't come out, being low XL seems to help here (or do I simply 
remember wrong?).

Put on my towel, went upstairs and let Medusa see that being a statue 
has advantages (for me ;). Well, then I was in a bind. No WoCold, no 
source of levitation or magical breathing, no flying pet to ride, no 
jumping, no ?oEarth, no Giants, no c!oGL...

Basically nothing to get across the Water back to the upstairs. Also no 
musical instrument to lower the castle drawbridge. And nothing to cross 
the moat.

That sucked, no way forward, no way back (I thought). I did have lots of 
food, so that was no worry, and so I decided to wait until some monster 
would be generated and hand me something to either lower the drawbridge, 
or get back up the dungeon.

I read the one unid'd scroll I had, it was remove curse so that didn't 
help much (had hoped for earth, obviously).

A magic trap on Medusa's island helped with monster generation and I 
might've gone back up already, since three winter wolf cubs got 
generated, but Stupidious appeared and ate my brain and I slew them all.

Tried a brass ring I found in one of the statues, but it was cursed and 
not leviataion... The pair of combat boots some monster dropped and 
which I put on (well, it could've been water walking or levitation), 
were cursed also, but no levitation and no water walking... Well, Tyr 
uncursed them for me when I #prayed and I got crowned as well.

Still, I was stuck and that sucked, I did break all the rest of the 
accesible statues and got some spellbooks, which weren't particularily 
useful (stone to flesh and detect monsmters), but in the process I 
remembered I had read a spellbook of forcebolt at some time. Unwearing 
my elven mithril coat and my helmet, I had a 64% fail force bolt, which 
opened the castle drawbridge. Now to cross the moat.

I had hoped for a giant handing me a boulder or a soldier with a WoCold 
or something in that direction, but nothing appeared. So, I decided to 
wait around a bit, lots of knives and spears and daggers flew my way, 
which I threw back a bit but mostly waited around.

Then I had an idea, the place you arrive at after falling into a pool of 
water is a bit randomized and the place where the drawbridge was, was 
sometimes empty. So, I dropped my bBoH, put most of the rustables into 
it and jumped into the water. A couple of tries later, I found myself on 
the other side, beset on all sides by evil beings. Xorns and lieutenants 
hit me up pretty bad, and I just barely made it back to the other side 
of the moat after three failed attempts at "semi-drowning" across.

Now I began throwing back stuff at the guys in the castle in earnest. 
First I teleported some of the monster away, but there were only 2 
charges left in my WoTeleport, and all the other attack wands were 
emptied pretty fast (I had two of magic missile and one of lightning).

So, I gathered an elven bow and some arrows lying around and fired those 
across. Then I emptied an arrow trap (too bad they changed the infinite 
arrow miling in 3.4.2) and shot those over the moat.

Then I dragged a total of 230 or so rocks from Medusa's level (no more 
statues on that level...) down and began casting the first rock. And the 
second and the third and ...(in batches of 50, being strained isn't such 
a good idea).

After some time I had stoned a pretty fair number of monsters on the 
castle side of the moat (I heard them say "Jehova" quite distinctly ;) 
and even got a point of dexterity for my troubles. :)

So, I again made my (wet) way over, after dropping my BoH in front of 
the moat. On the other side, I was still being beat up rather badly (an 
AC of -15 and 88 max HP with no OoF...), so I ran deeper into the 
castle, into the north side arm, (the corridor leading to the rooms 
where the chest is) were I was lucky enough to finaly get a boulder from 
a giant, so, after slaying that, I could block the entrance to the north 
corridor a bit and take out the remaining monsters one by one as they 
queued up there.

The only stupid thing about it was that the boulder was stuck in the 
corridor, otherwise I would've used it for the moat... Well, as it was, 
I went to the moat, crossed over again, tossed my BoH into the Castle, 
crossed yet again (rusting my (found) +3 helmet in the process, since I 
had forgotten to take it of that time) and went down into the VotD 
(didn't have that much choice, really).

The VotD was cleaned out without any major problems and the castle and 
the VotD yielded another two unid'd rings and two ?oID. And got me 
skilled in dagger, which helped against the one Lich and the 
Disenchanter bothering the neighbourhood... Plus I finally got enough XP 
to get to XL 14, so I could go do the quest, once I could get back to 
the Norn.

Well, one ?oID identified the three rings and one of the rings was 
uncursed levitation, which was pretty good (I wouldn't have wanted to do 
Gehennom at XL 14 searching for some levitation or WoCold or something). 
I rejoiced and cleared out the rest of the castle, getting a cloak of 
displacement in the process (I'm thinking of keeping that, it'll lower 
the chances of somebody death fingering me again, I should hope). Also 
two tins of spinach were aquired and I'm now back on Dlvl 15, sorting my 
stash at an attended altar of Tyr, getting ready for the Quest (which 
I'll do tomorrow, I'm getting  a bit sleepy and I don't want to blow 
this game now).

One thing I thought was cool about what happened was the endless amount 
of possibilities Nethack offers to get out of difficult situations. It's 
what I like most about the game. There's almost always a way to get the 
game along.
